ider_buying":0.938,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":93.8,"pf":[],"description_full":"Solaris Energy Infrastructure, Inc. provides modular and scalable equipment-based solutions for power generation, control and distribution, and management of raw materials used in the completion of oil and natural gas wells in the United States. It operates in Solaris Power Solutions and Solaris Logistics Solutions segments. The Solaris Power Solutions segment delivers power generation, control, and distribution solutions; and offers support to data center, energy, and other commercial and industrial sector. It also provides site preparation, specialized structural and foundational work, and gas pipeline construction services. The Solaris Logistics Solutions segment designs and manufactures specialized equipment; and offers field technician support, last mile, and mobilization logistics services, as well as provides software solutions. The company was formerly known as Solaris Oilfield Infrastructure, Inc. and changed its name to Solaris Energy Infrastructure, Inc. in September 2024. Solaris Energy Infrastructure, Inc. was founded in 2014 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William A. Zartler | Co-CEO, Founder & Chairman | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 468 people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 32%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Solaris Energy Infrastructure,  is a mid-cap energy business with a $6.1B market cap on $622M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -2.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 10% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The company is burning through $438M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 8.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 529% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.286961691237337},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (25.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.0pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 18% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (94% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Energy \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(SEI) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/SEI_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_112626043001_1795685401.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795685401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Solaris Energy Infrastructure (SEI) Shares Moved, What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-sei/solaris-energy-infrastructure/news/solaris-energy-infrastructure-sei-shares-moved-what-is-drivi","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795673599.171,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"William A. Zartler Acquires 4,000 Shares of Solaris Energy Infrastructure (SEI) Class A Stock at $53.11 on November 20, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/william-a-zartler-acquires-4000-shares-of-solaris-energy-infrastructure-sei-class-a-stock-at-5311-on-november-20-2026","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795206076.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]}